From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:27:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: mt6797-spm-sleep: optionally register the WFI
 state alone

With the CPU0 cpuidle driver registered, SODI test periods stopped
returning under inbound pings and the device reset (stages D5a, D5b).
Without it the same test passed (D5d). With two states, CPU0's idle
goes through the menu governor, which keeps the tick when it predicts
a short idle. With one state it skips the governor and stops the tick
as with no driver, but still enters through the cpuidle core.

Add sodi_idle_states (1 or 2, default 2) to split the two (D5e).
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
index 549f37466..dfd2eca33 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-spm-sleep.c
@@ -1162,6 +1162,14 @@ static bool sodi_idle = true;
 module_param(sodi_idle, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(sodi_idle, "SODI idle: register the CPU0 cpuidle driver");
 
+/*
+ * States to register: 2 (WFI and SODI) or 1 (WFI alone). With one state the
+ * idle loop skips the governor and stops the tick as with no driver (D5e).
+ */
+static unsigned int sodi_idle_states = 2;
+module_param(sodi_idle_states, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(sodi_idle_states, "SODI idle: states to register, 1 (WFI) or 2 (WFI, SODI)");
+
 static const u8 sodi_wake_bit[] = { 0, 2, 5, 6, 22 };
 static const char * const sodi_wake_name[] = {
 	"timer", "keypad", "conn2ap", "eint", "cirq",
@@ -1388,6 +1396,7 @@ static void sodi_idle_register(void)
 	s.idle.idle = true;
 	s.idle.flags = (s.flags & ~BIT(7)) | BIT(3) | SODI_FLAG_CG_MODE;
 	sodi_idle_driver.cpumask = (struct cpumask *)cpumask_of(0);
+	sodi_idle_driver.state_count = clamp(sodi_idle_states, 1U, 2U);
 	ret = cpuidle_register(&sodi_idle_driver, NULL);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_info(&s.pdev->dev, "cpuidle registration failed (%d)\n", ret);
-- 
2.43.0

